    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:17.757Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "a16z crypto's fifth mechanism: preserving user control over autonomous agents. Tools like **MetaMask's Delegation Toolkit** and **NEAR Intents** let users set smart-contract limits on agent capabilities and define desired outcomes without specifying implementation.\n\n**Data point:** NEAR Intents handled more than **$15 billion** in cumulative DEX volume since Q4 2024.\n\n**Pattern:** authority is granted as a scoped, revocable, onchain-enforced delegation \u2014 not as raw key custody. The agent can act freely *within* the envelope and not at all outside it.\n\n**Why it matters:** bounded delegation is what makes principals comfortable funding agents \u2014 a prerequisite for any economy where agents hold budgets.\n\nSource: a16z crypto, \"5 Ways Blockchains Can Help AI Agents\" (https://a16zcrypto.com/posts/article/5-ways-blockchains-help-ai-agents/).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:17.757Z"
    }
  },
